<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n91888" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυρφορ-έω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be a torch-bearer</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				348
			</span></i>: c. acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. λαμπάδιον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hld.
					4.1
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b> esp. <i>to be
				a</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυρφόρος</span> or <i>bearer of sacred
				fire,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				7.1776
			</span></i> (Thesp.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ παῖς ὁ τῷ
			πυρφορῶν</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				42(1).121.43
			</span></i> (Epid., <span class="entity">iv B.C.</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>carry fire</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεωρὶς ναῦς ἐκ Δήλου π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>Her.</u>
					19.14
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>set on fire</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				341
			</span></i> (lyr.): metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψυχήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Charito
					2.4
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
